WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.569
-Thank you very much for
watching "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.772
I appreciate it, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.140
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.275
Well, guys, the big news today
is that President Trump

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.678
has been released
from Walter Reed hospital.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.080
Here's a message
from his doctor earlier today.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.749 line:0%
-He's met or exceeded
all standard

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.716 line:0%
hospital discharge criteria.

00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:20.686 line:0%
He'll receive another
dose of Remdesivir here today,

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.788 line:0%
and then we plan to
get him home.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.792 line:0%
Though he may not entirely be
out of the woods yet,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.128 line:0%
the team and I agree that
all our evaluations,

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.830 line:0%
and, most importantly,
his clinical status

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.899 line:0%
support the president's
safe return home.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.834
-Yep. Good news?

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.070
It's safe for
the president to return home,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.570
mostly because everyone at
The White House

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.141
already has the virus.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.442
When she heard
he was coming home,

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:47.947
Melania immediately checked
herself into Walter Reed.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.148
But this was nice.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.517
The staff went all out
to welcome Trump home.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:52.885
They even hung
a bunch of balloons

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.455
that looked exactly like
the coronavirus.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.992
Yep, Trump left the hospital
for two reasons.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.326
One, he was feeling better.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.262
Two, he didn't want to
get billed for another night.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.697
[ As Trump ] I know
how these things work.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.132
[ Normal voice ]
A reporter then asked about

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:09.536
Trump's mental status, like if
he has any neurological symptoms

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:12.138
or fogginess as a result of
having the virus,

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.939
and here is what the doctor
had to say.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.843 line:0%
-I think you have seen
the videos and now the tweets,

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.911 line:0%
and you'll see him shortly.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:22.549 line:0%
You know, he's back, yeah.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.886
-The reporter was like,
"Yeah, we did.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.123
That's why we're asking you."

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.826
Some crazy times when you can
judge the president's health

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.927
from his videos and tweets.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:37.363 line:0%
This afternoon, Trump broke
the news on Twitter,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.765 line:0%
saying, "I'll be leaving the
great Walter Reed Medical Center

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.000 line:0%
today at 6:30.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.136 line:0%
Feeling really good.
Don't be afraid of COVID.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.737 line:0%
Don't let it dominate your life.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.706 line:0%
I feel better than I did
20 years ago."

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.576
I'm not surprised Trump feels
better than he did 20 years ago.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:54.980
Back then,
he was $800 million in debt.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.549
Trump left Walter Reed today,
but he actually left

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:00.186
the hospital for a little while
over the weekend. Watch.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.589 line:0%
-The president got in his S.U.V.
and went out

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.757 line:0%
to wave to supporters
gathered outside.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.460 line:0%
-He's there in the back seat,
wearing a mask and waving.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.063 line:0%
Others in the S.U.V.
with him exposed.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:13.499 line:0%
Health experts say the president
likely still contagious.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.503
-Yeah, according to
"The New York Times,"

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.037
Trump wanted to leave
the hospital,

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.306
and doctors wanted him
to stay inside,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:25.477
so they compromised,
and Trump left the hospital.

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.814
Yeah, the Secret Service
had to take Trump around

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:32.452
after 50 Uber XL drivers
were like, "Hell no."

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.620
What is happening?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.488
Trump even turned
a hospital stay into chaos.

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:41.260
The Joker caused less trouble
when he visited Gotham General.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.562
You could tell
the Secret Service

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.030
thought the joyride
was a bad idea.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.601
Right after, they went on eBay
looking for a used Popemobile.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.536
Well, it turns out
Trump's joyride

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.404
may have even his own
family thinking

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:53.639
he is acting irrationally.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.643
According to sources,
Don Jr. is deeply upset

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.677
by his father's decision
to drive around

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.946
and thinks Trump
is acting crazy.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.549
You know things have gone off
the rails when Don Jr.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.285
becomes the voice of reason.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.920
In response,
President Trump was like,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.288
"I'm not acting crazy,

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:13.826
and here's 15 all-caps tweets
to prove it."

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.627
Meanwhile, on Saturday night,
The White House

00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:18.731
released some photos to
show that Trump was busy working

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.166
while he was at Walter Reed.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.768
Here is one of
Trump signing a document.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.905
Could we zoom in on that?

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.639
People are saying that
he's just writing his name

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:29.709
on a blank piece of paper,
but that's not true.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.043
That's not true.

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:32.211
That's not
a blank piece of paper.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:37.650
That's just his entire plan
to stop COVID.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.420
It seems like a photo op,
but they've really just been

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.756
handing Trump blank pages to
sign for the past four years.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.190
"This is urgent, Mr. President."

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:48.861
[ As Trump ] Oh, well,
then I have to sign it.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.229
[ Normal voice ] Well,
some people online are calling

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.898
the announcement ceremony
for Amy Coney Barrett

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:56.101
"The Rose Garden Massacre"
after it's been identified as

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:57.303
the super-spreader event.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.972
Take a look.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.372
Yeah.

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:03.442
By the way, could those seats be
packed together any tighter?

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.044
Even the C.E.O. of Southwest
was like,

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.913
"Come on,
give him a little room."

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.349
Right after that photo,
Trump was like,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:13.085
"Okay, now let's all get
in a big pile."

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.520
Let's change gears.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.989
I saw that Coca-Cola announced
that they are discontinuing

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.425
their coconut-water brand Zico.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:23.296
It's a big blow for all of
those people who love pretending

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:27.032
that they like
the taste of coconut water.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:30.269
-Hey! Hey!

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.872
-Coca-Cola knew it was time
to discontinue Zico

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:37.142
because they actually did it
a year ago, and no one noticed.

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:38.544
And, finally, this is exciting.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:39.746
A pretty famous house
just got put on the market.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.046
Watch this.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:44.083 line:0%
-The house that played a central
role in the 1991 thriller

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.118 line:0%
"Silence of the Lambs"
is for sale

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.454 line:0%
for the price of
just under $300,000.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:52.224 line:0%
Fans of the movie can buy
the on-screen Pennsylvania home

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:54.526 line:0%
of the fictional serial killer
Buffalo Bill.

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:58.331
-Man, I know people are buying
a lot of houses right now,

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:01.433
but you've got to draw
the line somewhere, right?

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:03.036
Yeah, Realtors say
they'll be happy to give you

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:04.704
a tour of the front porch
and nothing else.

